  "headline": "Westpac's net profit excluding Notable Items (the bank's core cash-comparable measure) fell $141 million or 2% to $6,972 million in FY25 from $7,113 million in FY24. Statutory net profit declined $74 million or 1% to $6,916 million (FY24: $6,990 million). The smaller statutory decline reflected a $67 million improvement in hedging-related Notable Items (a $56 million reduction in FY25 versus $123 million in FY24). Total operating income rose 3% to $22,464 million (FY24: $21,763 million), driven by net interest income up $557 million (+3%) on 3% AIEA growth partly offset by 1 bps lower Core NIM, and non-interest income up $144 million (+5%). Pre-provision profit fell $271 million (3%) to $10,548 million. Lower impairment charges ($424 million vs $537 million, down $113 million) partially offset higher expenses ($11,916 million vs $10,944 million, up $972 million underlying plus $273 million restructuring). Tax and NCI contributed $17 million positively.",
